hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1083","Ali bin Hajar Al-Saadi told us, Ismail, meaning Ibn Jafar, told us, Muhammad, who is Ibn Abi Harmala, told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Dharr said: “My beloved advised me to do three things, which I will never give up, God willing, ever. He advised me to pray the forenoon prayer, to perform the Witr prayer before going to sleep, and to fast.” Three days of every month.” Abu Bakr said: Abu Hurairah reported: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, advised me to do three days that I took out in other than this place\""
"
